Main business: Setting out plan of action for foreseeable future. Action: Discussion and brainstorming.

Upon discussion of company name and model, preliminary company name “Recyclotronics” model name undecided. 

Roles were decided based on individual strengths and passions. 

Gripping mechanism discussed. 
    · Current driven tendril design suggested but concerns with time constraints and complexity were raised. Biomimicry was deemed convoluted. 
    · Crane was also mentioned but concerns surrounding efficiency, electromagnetic crane discussed as an offshoot concept. 
    · following on a pinching claw was developed. Storage of object. Picking up multiple was mentioned but software team have concerns regarding weight, size and sorting colour. One at a time 
    
Object 
    · Five different colour/recycle options but only choose three 
    · Shape and weight of box discussed with indents and hooks but team expressed desire for a more ambitious project involving a universally suitable shape, concerns about marketability also raised. 
    · Different shapes respective to different recyclable materials discussed but team are concerned ambitions are becoming bloated. 

Detection of Objects. 
    Ultrasonic sensors on all sides of buggy continually detecting, once object is within specified range, reverse motors to measure distance. 
    Pushing object also discussed but final verdict was reversing buggy. 
    Colour used to decipher between object and obstacle. 
    
Line following 
    · Memory system discussed but team worry this may be too complex 
    · Gyroscope and position detectors in two places also mentioned 
    · Double back once object grabbed to get onto line 
    · Position sensor used to negate line following on path back. This is an efficient and time saving idea theoretically, however, lines are hypothetical roads and charging through a straight 
    path not following roads is dangerous and destructive. 
    Environment Starting place will double as charging hub One object at a time or multiple All dump bins at base 
    
